     I glanced through the how-to and the associated
diff for the nethack sources.  I don't work with nethack
on Windows, either with or without Unix emulation, so
can't comment on that aspect.  As far as the diffs go,
instead of patching global.h, you ought to be able to
add `-DSKIP_BOOLEAN' to CFLAGS in your Makefile and use
whatever `boolean' is defined by the compiler's header
files rather than forcing gcc to see a compatible
duplication.  And the patch for mkmap.c is dealing with
a nethack source bug, but not making the correct fix;
that prototype ought to use `BOOLEAN_P' instead of
`?CHAR_P' for the two boolean arguments.




